WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.590
Local processing can keep most video and inference data under the operator's direct

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.360
control.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.660
This can support privacy goals, data residency, limited retention,

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.500
and clearer decisions about which event clips leave the site.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.950
It also reduces dependence on a third party's storage and model service.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.515
A local system can continue core analysis when internet connectivity is degraded or

00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:20.300
unavailable.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.760
Alerts may remain on the local dashboard until an external channel returns.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.580
This is useful for remote facilities, unreliable connections,

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.675
and environments where continuous cloud upload is impractical.

00:00:29.675 --> 00:00:33.360
Local workflows may reduce recurring bandwidth, storage, and inference charges,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.877
especially when many high-resolution streams are involved.

00:00:35.877 --> 00:00:39.925
They can also provide low-latency event handling because frames do not need a round trip

00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:41.130
to a remote service.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.040
The tradeoff is operational ownership.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.160
Local hardware has finite CPU, GPU, memory, power, and storage.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.125
The organization must size capacity, maintain drivers and models, monitor health,

00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:53.950
protect the host, and replace failed components.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.756
Accuracy does not improve merely because inference is local.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:59.620
Model choice, training data, camera placement, weather, lighting,

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.235
and threshold tuning still determine performance.

00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:06.170
Smaller models that fit the hardware may have different capabilities than larger hosted

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:06.920
services.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.385
Local and cloud processing can be combined selectively,

00:01:09.385 --> 00:01:11.040
but the data flow should be explicit.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.870
Choose architecture by privacy, reliability, cost, latency, capability,

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.400
and support requirements.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.365
The best design is the one the organization can operate securely and transparently,

00:01:20.365 --> 00:01:22.720
not simply the one with the most AI features.
